6 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198489 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198489 #edb/ref 1050 780.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198489 #edb/ref 1050 780.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186198489 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "64d036ec-bd13-5db0-909a-44c4f2ba1ce6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199248 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199314 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199248 #edb/ref 1061 26205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199248 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2f924b6e-2f47-553e-b2e6-6d98b8c55641" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199248 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199249 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199249 #edb/ref 1061 26206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199249 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "16b2c818-03e6-5801-97b2-0ce8d225c3d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199249 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199266 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199266 #edb/ref 1061 42404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199266 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "54cb06ef-1ffc-5b15-9147-a1baf70b985c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199266 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199460 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199268 #edb/ref 1061 42423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199268 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1b07afe2-9993-5d3c-bfe7-b98917224b3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199268 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199314 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199314 #edb/ref 1061 44589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199314 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "63b8e23b-b4a6-5984-b37f-dab9c1ced3af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199314 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199315 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199315 #edb/ref 1061 44598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199315 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "809a242a-d30e-5e4d-9b3e-fc6725358aac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199315 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199450 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider a transformation $\\mathbf T,$ given by\n\n![](images/fe/fefb7b82a6da1421bb96798fe6377e66199b50b8630dc396518927a0f3fe204b.svg)\n\nThe points in the $(u,v)$ plane where $\\mathbf T$ is *locally* non-invertible are known as **critical points**. \n\nWe've already seen that $\\mathbf T$ is locally non-invertible when the Jacobian determinant is zero. Therefore, the critical points of $\\mathbf T$ are the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial (x, y)}{\\partial (u, v)}=0.\n$$\n\n  \n\nLet's compute the critical points of the following transformation:\n\n![](images/8e/8e55b2da9a0c1fcf1ab901d361c50b652c906b92f0fcd4b158793f7782cfe5f4.svg)\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =4u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-6v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4u & -6v \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4u\\cdot 1-(-6v)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when the Jacobian equals zero. So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 4u-6v & =0 \\\\ 2u-3v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the critical points of $\\mathbf{T}$ consist of those points that lie on the line $2u-3v=0$  in the $uv$-plane, shown below. \n\n![](images/5c/5c544e3d3ecbdeaf7dc372b40ee0f37cb14e3ba292b8180a263c91103a9efe61.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199450 #edb/ref 1065 4312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199450 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5f47e688-774b-5c89-a90d-ead52a871598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199450 #edb/ref 1067 "Critical Points of Transformations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199460 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's now state the so-called **inverse function theorem** for single-variable functions:\n\n*If $f: U \\to \\Bbb R$ is continuously differentiable on an open set $U\\subseteq \\mathbb R,$ $f(a) = b$ and $f'(a)\\neq 0$ for $a\\in U,$ then*\n\n- *$f$ is invertible in some neighborhood of $a,$*\n\n- *$f^{-1},$ the inverse of $f,$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b,$ and*\n\n- *the derivative of $f^{-1}$ is given by* \n\n$$\n\\left(f^{-1}\\right)'(b) = \\dfrac{1}{f'(a)} =\\dfrac{1}{f'(f^{-1}(b))}\\,.\n$$\n\nTo explain this concretely, consider the graph below:\n\n![](images/4d/4dfd8b142b594a2ca4f0e39f9b8ca1e04018bf0efd63f9dc2235bd61e9f9d70e.png)\n\nIn this example, the function $f$ is continuously differentiable at $x=a$ and has a nonzero derivative. As a result, $f^{-1}$ exists in a neighborhood of $x=b$ and is continuously differentiable at this point.\n\nOn the other hand, if $f$ is continuously differentiable at $x=a$ but $f'(a) = 0,$ then one of two things can happen:\n\n- **Case 1**: The function $f$ does not have a local inverse at $a.$\n\n![](images/04/04ee310e6068e517aec42a67fa83837986f8807e1250b89b52e7a62e3975bb38.png)\n\nIn the example above, $f$ is not one-to-one in a neighborhood of $a,$ so it's not invertible there.\n\n- **Case 2**: The function $f$ has a local inverse at $a,$ but its inverse is not continuously differentiable at $b.$\n\n![](images/3e/3e2738a16f999d503fb295f4fd6535a854884468a4d190ffa537a4ec9295490c.png)\n\nIn the example above, $f$ is invertible in a neighborhood of $a,$ but $f^{-1}$ is not differentiable at $x=b$ since it has a vertical tangent at this point." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199460 #edb/ref 1065 7036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199460 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c45037f7-31c7-5911-a00d-edaa4c5b86e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199460 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199477 #edb/ref 1064 "The inverse function theorem can be generalized to transformations too. We state it below:\n\n*Let $\\mathbf T:U \\to \\Bbb R^2$ be a $C^1$ (continuously differentiable) transformation on an open set $U\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ where *\n![](images/82/829c083606df36014d5b5b078b80c1c0ff1edb72f981880b4a1a6a16affb32dc.svg)\n\n*Further, suppose that $(u_0,v_0)$ is **not** a critical point of $\\mathbf T.$* Then,\n\n- *$\\mathbf T$ is locally invertible at $(u_0,v_0),$*\n\n- *$\\mathbf T^{-1},$ the inverse of $\\mathbf T,$ is a $C^1$ function in a neighborhood of $(x_0,y_0),$ and*\n\n- *the Jacobian determinant of $\\mathbf T^{-1},$ denoted $\\dfrac{\\partial (u, v)}{\\partial (x, y)} ,$ is given by*\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial (u, v)}{\\partial (x, y)} = \\left( \\dfrac{\\partial (x, y)}{\\partial (u, v)} \\right)^{-1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199477 #edb/ref 1065 7678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199477 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "04daa2a7-b824-543f-b8d6-79a5b54e4799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199477 #edb/ref 1067 "The Inverse Function Theorem for Transformations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275895 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275895 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275895 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e8316c3-945b-5d09-a275-e0c583f57a17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276127 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{u}{v}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276127 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276127 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4969b933-9252-5d6c-99a3-2d0800a47ff5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276131 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the circle ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276131 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276131 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "49fc877d-2b64-58a0-a27d-95f261c0a7b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276162 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the lines $v=\\pm 2u.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276162 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276162 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4db3508a-8d7f-5449-9c40-7069ccf6fd53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276551 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{v}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276551 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276551 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "770127d5-5c20-5966-b228-70cc5f941617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276671 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=\\pm v.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276671 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276671 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "855bca3a-ff78-5604-b854-6c63d00bbe2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277111 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2uv}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277111 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277111 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b84e8d31-b0f2-5bc7-b250-aae11f693050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277250 #edb/ref 1080 "4v" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277250 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277250 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c7cce8a1-986b-5e0d-9d7a-5c50318cedd8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277286 #edb/ref 1080 "The only critical point is $(0,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277286 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277286 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb7df95b-b32d-5ca1-b866-576a47074953" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277324 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d0b7c50f-b475-5cd3-a478-644d87193dc4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277385 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{v}{u}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277385 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277385 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9290ebb-9e9d-5d8a-8ec2-a3ee34d8fd40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277401 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277401 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277401 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dbb6f0a5-bfd6-5a0f-aea6-85ae01e06079" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277403 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the line $v=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277403 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277403 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dbeaac23-e098-5ed2-b6ba-88b5f1f7e94f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277455 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277455 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277455 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1fd723e-649c-5294-ae81-2a842e9e6b1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277465 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{10}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277465 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277465 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e3ad5de4-55a8-578b-8fc5-a8a2b67c0b42" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186275895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277465 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277748 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0c2b48aa-f3d5-54e7-9a9a-986efee1cf0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186277987 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94528d39-40c7-5d22-bbd3-10b2d8db0c92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186276671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186277403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186277286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278059 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bc5c8f10-5fa6-51ed-b472-61ec07b1ffb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278306 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278306 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160460" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278306 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278306 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-{v}^{2} \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278306 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cb96d7dc-7f59-56fa-90d1-c2a71b2fab70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278306 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)=uv.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =-2v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & -2v \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot u-(-2v)\\cdot v \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}+2{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ 2({u}^{2}+{v}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}+{v}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}=0$ defines the point $(0,0)$ in the $uv$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278312 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186277748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278312 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160479" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278312 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278312 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the transformation $T:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)).$ The inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}(x,y)\\to (u(x,y),v(x,y))$ is given by\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x-2y \\\\ 3x+4y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the Jacobian determinant of $T.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278312 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1615e71e-cacf-55f4-8706-f141063daf67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278312 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $u(x,y)=x-2y$ and $v(x,y)=3x+4y.$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321553 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the line $u=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321553 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321553 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34ef2d77-bba0-583d-ab24-6864e8cb1120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321608 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the circle ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321608 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321608 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b6dc061-def5-52ec-97ef-1ebc1a91b58f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322563 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical po